\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For each positive integer n outside\{2,4,9\}, does $S_{n}$ have an irreducible complex representation V such that $V\otimes V$ contains every irreducible complex representation of $S_{n}$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For each positive integer n outside\{2,4,9\}, does $S_{n}$ have an irreducible complex representation V such that $V\otimes V$ contains every irreducible complex representation of $S_{n}$?

